## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical observability skills in a CNPA stack, ensuring candidates understand how to trace requests end-to-end rather than isolating individual components.

## Key Concepts

- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry across HTTP, database, Kafka, and Redis
- Trace propagation via W3C traceparent headers
- Sampling strategies that balance detail with performance overhead
- Backend visualization tools (Jaeger, Tempo) and troubleshooting workflows
- End-to-end verification under controlled test conditions

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry setup for Node.js HTTP API
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { HttpInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-http');
const { PgInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-pg');
const { KafkaInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-kafkajs');
const { RedisInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-ioredis');
const { JaegerExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-jaeger');
const { BatchSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  serviceName: 'cnpa-api',
  spanProcessor: new BatchSpanProcessor(new JaegerExporter()),
  instrumentations: [
    new HttpInstrumentation(),
    new PgInstrumentation(),
    new KafkaInstrumentation(),
    new RedisInstrumentation(),
  ],
});

sdk.start();
```

This instrumentation automatically propagates W3C Trace Context headers across all components, ensuring end-to-end trace continuity.

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests disciplined schema evolution in a CNPA pipeline—a common friction point for mature organizations scaling event-driven architectures.

## Key Concepts

- **Schema compatibility**: BACKWARD (consumers can read old data with new schema), FORWARD (producers can write new schema that old consumers understand)
- **Kafka Schema Registry**: Stores and enforces compatibility rules per subject
- **Dual-writes**: Temporarily write to both v1 and v2 paths during migration
- **Feature flags**: Control rollout percentage without code deploys
- **Canary criteria**: Define measurable thresholds before promoting
- **Rollback strategy**: Ensure v1 remains viable throughout transition
- **Observability**: Lag, latency, error rates, and data integrity checks

## Code Example

```javascript
const { Kafka } = require('kafkajs');
const { SchemaRegistry, AvroSchema } = require('@confluentinc/kafka-schema-registry');

const kafka = new Kafka({ brokers: ['kafka:9092'] });
const producer = kafka.producer();
const registry = new SchemaRegistry({ url: 'http://schema-registry:8081' });

async function publishWithDualWrite(event, featureFlags) {
  const v1Payload = serializeV1(event);
  const v2Schema = await registry.getLatestSchema('my-topic-value');
  const v2Payload = serializeV2(event, v2Schema);

  const messages = [{ topic: 'my-topic-v1', messages: [{ key: event.id, value: v1Payload }] }];

  if (featureFlags.enableV2Schema) {
    messages.push({ topic: 'my-topic-v2', messages: [{ key: event.id, value: v2Payload }] });
  }

  await producer.sendBatch(messages);
}

function validateCanaryMetrics(metrics) {
  const deserializationSuccess = metrics.deserializationErrors / metrics.totalEvents;
  const lagDelta = metrics.currentLag - metrics.baselineLag;
  const latencyImpact = metrics.p99Latency - metrics.baselineP99;

  return deserializationSuccess < 0.001 && lagDelta < 10 && latencyImpact < 5;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Introduces access control in a CNPA stack, a common beginner-friendly area with real-world implications.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC, middleware, JWT validation
- Log redaction and PII protection
- Unit/integration tests, basic load testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-style middleware sketch
function rbac(requiredRoles){
  return (req,res,next)=>{
    const token=req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
    const payload=verifyJwt(token); // assume helper
    if(!payload || !requiredRoles.includes(payload.role)) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
    req.user=payload; next();
  };
}
```

